  "decision_conditions": [
    "The submitted existing and proposed rear elevations inaccurately illustrate the position of the existing two-storey rear projection and are inconsistent with the floor plans and the established arrangement of the property. The drawings therefore fail to provide an accurate and coherent representation of the existing building and proposed development, preventing the Local Planning Authority from properly assessing its design and neighbouring amenity impacts. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies 53 and 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "By reason of its excessive 2.8m eaves height, bulk and close relationship with the adjoining properties within a particularly narrow plot, the proposed wraparound extension would appear unduly dominant and monolithic and would result in an unacceptable sense of enclosure and loss of daylight and sunlight to neighbouring occupiers. The proposal would therefore be contrary to Policies 53 and 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024) and the adopted Residential Alterations and Retrofit Supplementary Planning Document (2026)."
  ],
